      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Well, I came in because... I just feel like I cannot settle inside my own skin anymore. It's like I have to jump up and do the next thing, even when I'm completely worn out and I really should just be sitting still. I tried to sit in my recliner yesterday to rest—it’s this lovely blue chair I got on sale at Macy's years ago, back when they actually had good sales, you know? The quality of furniture these days is just terrible, everything is made of that cheap particle board. My sister bought a coffee table last month and the leg snapped right off the very first day! She was so mad she drove it right back to the store in her trunk and made them give her a refund in cash. But... wait, what was I saying? Oh, right. I was trying to sit in my chair, and I just couldn't. I'm so tired, but my body just makes me get up and find something else to do.",
