    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you recently started any new medications or had a dose changed?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, no new pills. Everything is exactly the same as it's been. I just get my regular refills at the CVS down on Main Street. Although, I've really been thinking about switching pharmacies because the line at the drive-thru is always wrapped all the way around the building. Last time I went, I was sitting behind this silver Honda for twenty minutes! The woman driving was just chatting away with the pharmacist through the window like they were at a coffee shop. \n\nWhich reminds me, I really miss when pharmacies had those little soda fountains in them. When I was a little girl, my grandmother used to take me to the Rexall drug store and buy me a cherry vanilla float. You just can't find ice cream like that anymore. Everything now is all artificial flavors and high fructose corn syrup. It's no wonder everyone's stomach is always upset these days, nobody eats real food. I try to buy organic when I can, but the prices at the grocery store are just outrageous. A carton of eggs is practically the price of a steak! \n\nBut... oh, what were you asking me? Did I change my medicine? No, no, it's all the same.",
