    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "{\"intent\": \"Determine if there is a history of past depressive episodes to distinguish bipolar disorder from a single manic episode.\", \"question\": \"Have you ever had a period in the past where you felt deeply down or depressed for weeks at",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Depressed? No, I don't think so. I mean, I'm not really a down-in-the-dumps kind of person. I do get a little sad when I watch the evening news sometimes, though. The news is just so terrible lately, isn't it? My neighbor, Margaret, she watches those 24-hour news channels all day long and she is just miserable all the time. I told her she needs to turn that television off and go plant some petunias or something. Gardening is so good for you. \n\nI tried to grow beefsteak tomatoes last summer, but the squirrels kept taking exactly one bite out of the green ones and leaving them sitting on the fence! They are such a nuisance. I went down to the hardware store to buy some of that chicken wire to keep them out, but the boy working in the garden center had no idea where anything was. He was just a teenager, probably his very first job, poor thing. Kids these days just don't get trained properly at all. Management just hands them an apron and says good luck. It's a shame, really. \n\nBut... oh dear, I lost my train of thought again. What did you ask me? Was I depressed? No, no, I've never felt deeply down for weeks at a time or anything like that. Just this awful restless feeling I told you about.",
